.TH STEGOFORGE 1 "2026-10-22" "StegoForge 1.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stegoforge \- steganography toolkit (encode/decode/detect/ctf/capacity/diff/batch/web)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stegoforge encode -c CARRIER -p PAYLOAD [-k KEY | --key-file F] [--allow-plaintext] [--pad-to N] [--require-v2] [--enforce-strong-pass] [--no-magic] [--depth 1-4] [--method M] [--wet-paper] [--target T] [--test-survival] [--decoy D --decoy-key K]
.br
.B stegoforge decode -f STEGO [-k KEY | --key-file F] [--method M] [--require-v2] [--wet-paper]
.br
.B stegoforge detect -f FILE [--chi2] [--rs] [--exif] [--blind] [--ml] [--fingerprint] [--binary] [--all] [--case-id ID] [--stdin]
.br
.B stegoforge ctf -f FILE [--batch DIR] [--no-save] [--output-dir D] [--case-id ID] [--stdin]
.br
.B stegoforge capacity -c CARRIER [--method M] [--depth N]
.br
.B stegoforge diff -c COVER -s STEGO [--save-heatmap P]
.br
.B stegoforge batch -d DIR -p PAYLOAD -k KEY [--jobs N] [--method M] [--depth N]
.br
.B stegoforge survive -c CARRIER -p PAYLOAD -k KEY --target T
.br
.B stegoforge web [--port N] [--host H]
.br
.B stegoforge deadrop post -c C -p P -k K [--upload-url U]
.br
.B stegoforge deadrop check --url U -k K
.br
.B stegoforge deadrop monitor --url U -k K [--interval S]
.br
.B stegoforge deadrop keyx initiate -c C -o OUT [--local-passphrase P] [--sign-key-file F]
.br
.B stegoforge deadrop keyx complete -f F [--local-passphrase P] [--verify-key-file F] [--output-key-file O] [--legacy-v1]
.br
.B stegoforge schema [NAME] [--json]
.br
.B stegoforge completion [bash|zsh|fish]
.br
.B stegoforge init
.br
.B stegoforge doctor [--json]
.br
.B stegoforge update [--check-only] [-y]
.SH DESCRIPTION
StegoForge hides encrypted payloads in image, audio, video, document, and
binary carriers, and provides forensic detectors for CTF and research use.
Encryption is AES-256-GCM with Argon2id (v2 method-bound AAD by default;
legacy v1 still decodes unless
.B --require-v2
is given). Without a key, encoding is refused unless
.B --allow-plaintext
.RB ( or
.BR --no-encrypt )
is passed. See docs/API.md, docs/PROTOCOL.md, docs/METHODS.md, docs/ERRORS.md.
.PP
Exit status is 0 on success, 1 on usage/operation errors (JSON mode prints
{"status": "error", ...}).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -k ", " --key
Passphrase. Visible in process list; prefer
.B --key-file
or the STEGOFORGE_KEY environment variable.
.TP
.B --key-file F
Read passphrase from file F.
.TP
.B --pad-to N
Pad plaintext to N-byte blocks (1-256) before encryption.
.TP
.B --no-magic
Use a key-derived header instead of the static SFRG magic (encode only;
incompatible with decoy mode).
.TP
.B --i-understand-root
Acknowledge authorization for live network covert-channel operations.
.TP
.B --no-save
CTF triage without writing extracted payloads (read-only forensics).
.TP
.B --case-id ID
Forensic case identifier recorded in detect/ctf reports.
.TP
.B --offline
Skip network bootstrap (same as STEGOFORGE_OFFLINE=1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STEGOFORGE_KEY
Key fallback (inherited by child processes; prefer --key-file).
.TP
.B STEGOFORGE_ALLOW_PLAINTEXT
Set to 1 to allow keyless embeds without --allow-plaintext.
.TP
.B STEGOFORGE_WEB_TOKEN
Require token for web UI (use value "auto" for a per-boot token on stderr).
.TP
.B STEGOFORGE_OFFLINE / STEGOFORGE_OFFLINE_FONTS
Skip bootstrap / remote fonts.
.TP
.B STEGOFORGE_UPDATE_SHA256 / STEGOFORGE_UPDATE_SIG_URL / STEGOFORGE_UPDATE_UNPINNED
Self-update verification pins.
.TP
.B STEGOFORGE_MODEL_SHA256 / STEGOFORGE_FFMPEG_SHA256
Asset integrity pins.
.TP
.B STEGOFORGE_LLM_TOKEN / STEGOFORGE_ALLOW_PRIVATE_LLM
Linguistic LLM auth / private-endpoint opt-in.
.TP
.B STEGOFORGE_I_UNDERSTAND_ROOT
Non-interactive equivalent of --i-understand-root.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.stegoforge/bin, ~/.stegoforge/models
(asset cache),
.I stegoforge_ops/schemas/json-schema.json
(machine schemas),
.I assets.sha256
(release asset hashes).
.SH SEE ALSO
docs/API.md, docs/PROTOCOL.md, docs/THREAT-MODEL.md, docs/OPENAPI.md
